NAME
     traceroute - the path to a host

SYNOPSIS
     traceroute [-n] [-q TRIES] [-m MAXHOPS] HOST

DESCRIPTION
     traceroute sends packets with a small time-to-live and prints who
     sends back the "time exceeded" for each hop, which is the route to
     HOST as the network sees it.

OPTIONS
     -n          numbers rather than names
     -q TRIES    how many packets per hop
     -m MAXHOPS  how far to go

SEE ALSO
     ping(1), ip(8)
